// Survival combat scenario for Worldwake.
//
// Purpose: keep the survival loop alive while a capable guard pursues a known
// hostile at an authored bandit camp, kills the camp's only living member, and
// lets the camp system abandon the now-empty camp through its faction policy.
//
// Lawful competing affordances intentionally constrained:
// - one guard owns the survival-health envelope; the bandit is a supporting
//   hostile camp member
// - food and water are available at both places so the owned proof is combat
//   and camp aftermath rather than starvation pathfinding
// - patrol and pursuit profiles are inactive; combat is driven by same-place
//   hostility and local observation
(
    seed: 790415,
    survival_health_contract: (
        max_authored_critical_run_ticks: 170,
        max_idle_window_ticks_with_elevated_need: 50,
